+### Departures
+
+Each row names one declaration the built cascade writes differently from Bootstrap 5.3.8, keyed the
+way the official inventory is keyed: the component, the selector, the property, and the at-rule
+enclosing the declaration. One table follows per component, in the order the shipped keys sort.
+`readDepartures` in `tests/setupServer.ts` reads every one of them, and `collectDepartures` measures
+the same comparison over the unminified compile, so the conformance proof reddens on a difference no
+row records and on a row no difference carries.
+
+A `—` in `Condition` records a declaration under no at-rule, and a `—` in `Veneer` records a
+property this cascade leaves without a value, whether it omits the declaration or writes it empty.
+The `Departure` cell names why the two values differ: `tokenized` routes the release value through a
+Veneer token, `aliased` reads another compatibility variable in its place, `declared` writes a
+different value on purpose, `fallback` keeps the release value behind a `var()` fallback, and
+`dropped` leaves the declaration out.
+
